{"op": "insert_after", "segment": 19, "text": "20. Notice of immunity: Under 18 U.S.C. §1833(b), an individual shall not be held criminally or civilly liable under any federal or state trade secret law for the disclosure of a trade secret that (a) is made in confidence to a federal, state or local government official, either directly or indirectly, or to an attorney, solely for the purpose of reporting or investigating a suspected violation of law; or (b) is made in a complaint or other document filed in a lawsuit or other proceeding, if such filing is made under seal. An individual who files a lawsuit for retaliation by an employer for reporting a suspected violation of law may disclose the trade secret to the individual's attorney and use the trade secret information in the court proceeding, if the individual files any document containing the trade secret under seal and does not disclose the trade secret, except pursuant to court order.", "fixes": "LAW-DTSA-1833B, P-28"},
{"op": "delete", "segment": 16, "text": "", "fixes": "P-09"},
{"op": "replace", "segment": 11, "text": "6. The Recipient will, on request from the Discloser, return all copies and records of the Confidential Information to the Discloser and will not retain any copies or records of the Confidential Information, except that the Recipient may make and keep copies of Confidential Information to the extent needed for backup and disaster recovery purposes and to meet legally required record-keeping obligations, provided that such copies remain subject to this Agreement.", "fixes": "P-29"}
]}

{"scenarios": [
{"obligation_avoided": "Restriction on copying Confidential Information that is held in electronic or other intangible form", "segments": [61], "quotes": ["shall not duplicate Confidential Information furnished in tangible form"], "how": "The duplication restriction reaches only tangible copies, so the Recipient can argue it may freely copy information received electronically (files, data, code) into its own systems and keep those copies.", "loophole_type": "retained_copies"},
{"obligation_avoided": "Protection of health and other personal or third-party data that the Discloser holds but that is not proprietary to the Parties", "segments": [25, 28], "quotes": ["any data or information that is proprietary to the Parties and not generally known to the public", "Protected Health Information in both physical and electronic form"], "how": "The lead-in limits Confidential Information to data proprietary to the Parties, so the Recipient can argue that PHI and similar data owned by others falls outside the definition despite the enumerated list.", "loophole_type": "other"},
{"obligation_avoided": "Restriction on using the Confidential Information for purposes other than the Transaction after the Agreement ends", "segments": [45, 81], "quotes": ["The Parties agree to use the Confidential Information solely in connection with the Transaction", "Confidential Information that was disclosed during term"], "how": "Only the duty to hold information in confidence is stated to survive, and only for information disclosed during the term; the use restriction is not stated to survive, so after the term the Recipient can argue it may use the information freely.", "loophole_type": "short_term"},
{"obligation_avoided": "Effective injunctive relief against misuse of the Discloser's Confidential Information", "segments": [83, 84], "quotes": ["could cause irreparable harm to the Party and the general public", "the Parties shall be entitled to injunctive relief"], "how": "Harm is described only as something that could occur and no presumption of irreparable harm or bond waiver is stated, so the Recipient can contest each request on irreparable harm and treat the remedy as optional.", "loophole_type": "weak_remedy"},
{"obligation_avoided": "Protection against onward sharing of information with agents or representatives who have not signed any confidentiality undertaking", "segments": [38], "quotes": ["to its directors, officers, employees, agents or representatives", "who have a need to know such Confidential Information in connection with the Transaction"], "how": "The Recipient decides for itself who has a need to know and may pass the information to agents or representatives, and the draft requires no written confidentiality undertaking from them, so no binding duty is placed on the people who receive it.", "loophole_type": "other"},
{"obligation_avoided": "Protection of information that the Recipient claims it received from a third party", "segments": [69], "quotes": ["was received by the Recipient without breach of this Agreement from a third party"], "how": "The Recipient can assert that any information came from a third party, and this exclusion has no requirement for written records (unlike the independent-development exclusion), so it need not prove the source.", "loophole_type": "other"}
]}

